  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>Add the @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.oGbDwnLOn3isPJpO]{Impassioned Zeal} and @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.XU7D9CCmumuhqDUi]{Public Speaker} Talents to any career you enter. You may attempt an <strong>Opposed Leadership/Willpower Test</strong> to recruit people of Brass Status or who fall under the Peasant Class as @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-nom.nom-journals.JournalEntry.trUWzGkEqCbeCzvo.JournalEntryPage.svAtyhh8hprchwVv]{Bretonnian Man-At-Arms} to accompany you in battles as a united fighting force under your banner. The amount determined is based on your levels in @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.XU7D9CCmumuhqDUi]{Public Speaker} and the amount of people you can influence at a time plus the SL of the Test (WHFRP 4E Core Rulebook page. 142). If you have the @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.x8g3U68oi8XzWiYr]{Commanding Presence} Talent, you may roll your Leadership Test unopposed against those who respect your authority. With @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.QyjWtSdnVMT04l5Y]{Bless (The Lady)}, you may also grant any Blessing of the Lady for all Men-At-Arms recruited as if they were a single entity. Stats and equipment for Men-At-Arms are determined by the GM.</p>\n<p><strong>Grail Virtue :</strong> You gain a permanent +5 bonus to your Strength and Toughness Characteristics this does not count towards your Advances; moreover, you gain the @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.SfUUdOGjdYpr3KSR]{Regenerate} Trait and the @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.3wCtgMDNnu8MFmyk]{Immunity (Corruption, Disease, Fatigue, Poison)} Trait.</p>"
    },
